      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum.\n\n- The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. That is usually given as 850 mg three times daily, or up to 1,000 mg per dose.\n- Extended-release metformin has a maximum of 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day, depending on the formulation.\n- At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Possible intended doses include:\n- 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day)\n- 500 mg three times daily\n- 1,000 mg twice daily\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into divided doses\n\nPlease tell me the dose you intended, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is deliberate and give me the clinical rationale. Once you do, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
